# Runtime artifact dirs. Anchored to each known project root that produces them
# rather than a broad **/runtime/<sub>/ glob: an un-anchored glob would also match
# the tracked source/test trees app/runtime/ and tests/runtime/ and silently hide
# any future file added under e.g. tests/runtime/panel/ or app/runtime/settings/.
# Repo root:
# No trailing slash on runtime/settings: the compiler publishes it as a SYMLINK
# to the winning .settings.staged-* dir, and git treats a symlink as a file, so a
# directory-only pattern ("/runtime/settings/") does not match it and leaves
# `?? runtime/settings` in git status. The leading / keeps it anchored.
/runtime/settings
/runtime/builderops/
/runtime/dispatcher/
/runtime/orientation/
/runtime/panel/
/runtime/agent_memory/
/runtime/eval/
/runtime/relevance/
/runtime/activation/
# YouTube OAuth token ciphertext and the dev connect lease are app-local
# runtime state. Keep this narrowly anchored so app/knowledge_acquisition and
# tests/knowledge_acquisition remain fully visible to Git.
/runtime/knowledge_acquisition/
# Settings-compiler swap artifacts written as dot-prefixed *siblings* of
# runtime/settings/ (app/settings/compiler.py): .settings.lock, .settings.next,
# .settings.previous, and .settings.staged-* temp dirs. The /runtime/settings/
# entry above does not cover these, and a leftover runtime/.settings.lock is
# exactly what dirtied `git status --porcelain` on the #3891/#3892 branch.
/runtime/.settings.*
# companion-ui/companion-app (companion_ui tests run from this cwd and write
# runtime/panel/panel_confirmation.sqlite3 etc. relative to it):
/companion-ui/companion-app/runtime/settings
/companion-ui/companion-app/runtime/builderops/
/companion-ui/companion-app/runtime/dispatcher/
/companion-ui/companion-app/runtime/orientation/
/companion-ui/companion-app/runtime/panel/
/companion-ui/companion-app/runtime/agent_memory/
/companion-ui/companion-app/runtime/.settings.*
# Promotion-plan receipts are local ops artifacts, not repo truth (#2081).
# Scoped to ops/promotions/ and ops/test-promotions/ only — tracked ops/** siblings (benchmarks, observability, quality) stay tracked.
ops/promotions/
ops/test-promotions/
verification_report.md

